.Dd March 2, 2026
.Dt ELF_INIT_IA64 3
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm elf_init_ia64
.Nd initialize a writable ELF relocatable object for IA-64
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libelfobj
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In elfobj.h
.Ft elfobj_t *
.Fn elf_init_ia64 void
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn elf_init_ia64
function creates a new mutable
.Vt elfobj_t
configured for IA-64 relocatable objects.
.Pp
The returned object is initialized as:
.Bl -tag -width "Machine"
.It Type
.Dv ET_REL
.It Machine
EM_IA_64
.It Class
ELFCLASS64
.It Endian
ELFDATA2LSB
.It Flags
EF_IA_64_ABI64
.El
.Pp
The object includes default
.Pa .text ,
.Pa .data ,
and
.Pa .bss
sections with architecture-appropriate alignment.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn elf_init_ia64
function returns a pointer to a new object on success.
Otherwise, it returns NULL.
.Sh ERRORS
A NULL return indicates allocation or initialization failure.
.Sh EXAMPLE
.Bd -literal
#include <elfobj.h>

int
main(void)
{
    elfobj_t *obj = elf_init_ia64();
    if (obj == NULL)
        return 1;

    /* add sections/symbols/relocations, then write */
    elf_close(obj);
    return 0;
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr elfobj 3 ,
.Xr elf_section 3 ,
.Xr elf_symbol 3 ,
.Xr elf_reloc 3
